  "body": "## What\n\nAdds `anthropic` — MCC's first first-party Claude provider, speaking Anthropic's native Messages API at `api.anthropic.com` with a **Claude Console API key**, billed per token.\n\nMCC had **54 providers and none was Anthropic**. Claude was only reachable second-hand (resold via Kilo/Nous/Cline, or through Bedrock/Vertex). This closes that gap.\n\nThis is the authentication method Anthropic documents for software calling Claude on a user's behalf — see [Claude Code → Legal and compliance](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance):\n\n> Developers building products or services that interact with Claude's capabilities … should use API key authentication through Claude Console or a supported cloud provider.\n\n## Mechanism\n\nThe neutral Messages transport already existed from the Command Code work, but hardcoded `Authorization: Bearer` — Command Code's contract. Anthropic's own API needs `x-api-key` plus a required `anthropic-version` header.\n\nSo `AnthropicMessagesProvider` now takes an **injected auth strategy** rather than growing a second copy of the streaming loop. `BearerTokenAuth` remains the default, so Command Code's wire behaviour is unchanged and pinned by a regression test.\n\n## One real bug caught before it shipped\n\nThe upstream base URL is bound to **`ANTHROPIC_UPSTREAM_BASE_URL`**, deliberately *not* `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`.\n\n`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` is the variable that points Claude Code **at** MCC. Had the provider read it, every user who followed our own setup docs would have had the proxy dial its own listener and loop forever. A test pins the binding and carries the reason.\n\n## No invented metadata\n\nAnthropic's `/v1/models` publishes no context length, pricing, or capability flags. Every optional field is left `None` — \"not reported\", not \"absent\" — so models.dev enrichment can fill it and vision routing won't divert on merely-unknown image support (Part IV.1).\n\n## Verification\n\n| Layer | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| New tests | 15 passed |\n| Full suite | **4185 passed**, 26 skipped |\n| Failures | **6**, all `tests/scripts/test_installers.py` PowerShell — the documented irreducible baseline, identical to unmodified `main`. No installer file touched. |\n| ruff format / check / ty / suppression grep | clean |\n\n**Both load-bearing guards were mutation-tested** and confirmed to fail *by name*:\n\n```\nbind field back to ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL  -> test_upstream_base_url_does_not_read_anthropic_base_url FAILED\nApiKeyAuth emits a bearer token        -> 3 header assertions FAILED\n```\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **No live request has been made against `api.anthropic.com`** — there is no Console key on this machine. Request construction, header shape, model-list parsing and failure classification are tested; a real round trip is not. First user with a key is the real test.\n- `anthropic` is inserted first in `PROVIDER_CATALOG`. That order is display-only (\"UI and error-message listing\", `provider_catalog.py:767`) and has no routing effect — verified before choosing the position.\n- Reviewers: the local suite has 6 pre-existing PowerShell installer failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
