    },
    "message": "feat(providers): first-party Anthropic Messages provider (Console API key)\n\nMCC had 54 providers and none of them was Anthropic. Claude models were only\nreachable second-hand -- resold through Kilo/Nous/Cline, or via Bedrock and\nVertex -- so there was no way to point the proxy at api.anthropic.com with your\nown Console key. This adds that provider.\n\nMechanism. The native Messages transport already existed neutrally from the\nCommand Code work (providers/anthropic_messages), but it hardcoded\n`Authorization: Bearer` because that is Command Code's contract. Anthropic's own\nAPI authenticates with `x-api-key` and requires an `anthropic-version` header on\nevery request, so the transport now takes an injected auth strategy and the\ncredential shape becomes a per-upstream concern instead of a second copy of the\nstreaming loop. `BearerTokenAuth` is the default, so Command Code's wire\nbehaviour is byte-identical and guarded by a test.\n\nThe upstream base URL is deliberately bound to ANTHROPIC_UPSTREAM_BASE_URL, NOT\nANTHROPIC_BASE_URL. The latter is the variable that points Claude Code AT this\nproxy; had the provider read it, any user who had set it -- which is every user\nwho followed our own setup docs -- would have made the proxy dial its own\nlistener and loop. There is a test pinning that binding with the reason.\n\nModel listing reads GET /v1/models. Anthropic publishes no context length,\npricing, or per-model capability flags, so every optional field is left None\nrather than guessed: None means \"not reported\", which is what lets the\nmodels.dev enrichment fill it and stops vision routing diverting a model whose\nimage support is merely unknown (Part IV.1 -- no invented values).\n\nVerification.\n- 15 new tests; full suite 4185 passed, 26 skipped.\n- 6 failures, all tests/scripts/test_installers.py PowerShell tests -- the\n  documented irreducible baseline, identical to unmodified fork/main, and no\n  installer file was touched.\n- Both load-bearing guards mutation-tested and confirmed to fail by name:\n  binding the field back to ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL fails the loop guard; making\n  ApiKeyAuth emit a bearer fails three header assertions.\n- ruff format, ruff check, ty, and the suppression grep all clean.\n\nNot done: no live request has been made against api.anthropic.com -- there is no\nConsole key on this machine. Request construction, header shape, model-list\nparsing and failure classification are tested; a real round trip is not.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
